.TH ORO-COOKIES 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:cookies \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:cookies'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
WebView cookie helpers backed by the native platform cookie store.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBget(url)\fR
Get cookies for a URL as a `Cookie` header value ("a=b; c=d").
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIurl\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<{ value: string }>\fR
.TP
\fBset(url, cookie)\fR
Set a cookie for a URL from a `Set\-Cookie` header value.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIurl\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIcookie\fR (string; required) a Set\-Cookie header value
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<{ ok: boolean }>\fR
.TP
\fBremove(url, name)\fR
Remove cookies matching `name` for a URL.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIurl\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<{ ok: boolean }>\fR
.TP
\fBclear()\fR
Clear all cookies in the current WebView data store.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<{ ok: boolean }>\fR
